        <item>
            <title>0.2.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:21:11 +0000</pubDate>
            <link>https://danielyan.github.io/fresco-releases/</link>
            <sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>https://danielyan.github.io/fresco-releases/</sparkle:fullReleaseNotesLink>
            <sparkle:version>80</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Fresco 0.2.0</h2>
<pre>
Fresco 0.2.0 — settings you can keep with your dotfiles.

Fresco&#x27;s settings now live in ~/.config/fresco/config.json, and your
API keys in ~/.config/fresco/credentials.json (readable only by you).
Keep them alongside your other configuration and a new Mac can start
out set up the way you like it.

- Your current settings and keys move over automatically the first
  time 0.2.0 starts; there is nothing to do
- Edits to the files are picked up while Fresco is running
- Sign-ins to DeviantArt and Flickr stay on each Mac, so a new Mac
  asks you to connect those once
</pre>
]]></description>
